          %h3#AndAndLocalVersion Global (“non-covariant”) and local (“covariant”) version
          %p
            Functorial QFT in any dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            was originally formulated (
            %a{:href => "#Atiyah88"}> Atiyah 88
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Segal04"} Segal 04
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            on a 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cobordisms"}> category of cobordisms
            \. In this formulation, there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            assigned to every global spatial slice of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            into space and time components breaks
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+covariance"} general covariance
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+field+theories"} topological quantum field theories
            to which the methods of FQFT apply most immediately.
          %p
            A local (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"}> extended
            ”, “multi-tiered”) refinement of this is naturally given by passing from 1-functors to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-functors"} (∞,n)-functors
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-categories+of+cobordisms"} (∞,n)-categories of cobordisms
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BaezDolan95"} Baez-Dolan 95
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Luire09"} Lurie 09
          %h2#Introduction Exposition and Introduction
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
          %p
            We give here motivation for, introduction to and an exposition of the ideas of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+quantum+field+theory"} local
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"}> extended
            ) functorial field theory.
          %p We start in
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#QuantumMechanicsInSchroedingerPicture"} Quantum mechanics in Schrödinger picture
          %p by showing how all the basic category-theoretic ideas are already right beneath the surface of the traditional textbook discussion of quantum mechanics. Following that in
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#PathIntegralQuantizationof1dGaugeTheory"} Path integral quantization of 1d gauge theory
          %p
            we show for the simple case of 1-dimensional finite gauge theory how also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral+quantization"} path integral quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"}> classical
            ) data is naturally organized by monoidal category theory with first bits of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            showing up (that will play a more paramount role as one goes up in dimension).
          %p Then in
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#QMWithInteractionAndFeynmanDiagrams"} Quantum mechanics with interaction and Feynman diagrams
          %p
            this becomes all the more pronounced when one considers quantum mechanics with interaction as in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline+formalism"} worldline formalism
            and hence when one considers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
            as diagrams of interactions of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
          %p
            This 1-dimensional functorial description worldline quantum mechanics has an evident generalization to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            formulation of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+topological+field+theory"} 2d topological field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Global2dTQFT"} Naive generalization: Global 2d TQFT
          %p
            However, this “naive” generalization is not quite refined enough. Physically one sees this from the fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+string"} topological string
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-model"} A-model
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"} B-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+TQFT"} 2d TQFT
            in physics, is not actually an instance of the Atiyah-Segal axiomatics. Mathematically one sees it from the fact that the 1-category theoretic formulation of 2d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            is clearly lacking a “categorical dimension” in order to be satisfactory.
          %p
            The correct refinement of 2d TQFT to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomological+field+theory"} cohomological field theory
            or “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TCFT"}> TCFT
            ” with coefficients not just in vector spaces but in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            of vector spaces we then consider in
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Local2dTQFT"} Local2dTQFT – The topological string
          %p
            This gives a natural conceptual home to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+categories"} derived categories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            famous from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+mirror+symmetry"} homological mirror symmetry
          %p
            To get a feeling for what is missing, we next consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+TQFT"} 3d TQFT
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#Global3dTQFT"} Global 3d TQFT – Chern-Simons theory
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#Local3dTQFT"} Local 3d TQFT – Modular functor and Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
          %p
            This finally is enough information to naturally motivate the full formulation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2Cn%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,n)-category
            theory in
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#IntroductionGeneralFormulation"} General local TQFT
          %h3#QuantumMechanicsInSchroedingerPicture Quantum mechanics in Schrödinger picture
          %p
            This section introduces the observation that the basic structures in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            are accurately reflected in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
