          %h4#TimeEvolutionAndFunctors Time evolution and Functors
          %p
            The basic idea of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            in the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+picture"}> Schrödinger picture
            ” is to describe a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanical+system"} quantum mechanical system
            (such as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            of a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proton"} proton
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                assigning to each time
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in \mathbb{R}
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"}> Hilbert space
                )
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_t
                to be thought of as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
                (of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+states"} pure states
            %li
              %p
                assigning to each pair
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [t_1,t_2]
                of times a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operator"} linear operator
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"}> unitary operator
                )
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
