          #GroupoidsAsHomotopy1Types.num_defn
            %h6#definition_notation Definition (Notation)
            %p Here and in the following, the convention is that we write
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
                  (with the subscript decoration) when we regard groupoids with just homomorphisms (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"}> functors
                  ) between them,
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
                  (without the subscript decoration) when we regard groupoids with homomorphisms (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"}> functors
                  ) between them and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"}> natural transformations
                  ) between these
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↗
                                %msup
                                  %mo ↘
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi f
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⇓
                              %mtd
                                %mi Y
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↘
                                %msub
                                  %mo ↗
                                  %mi g
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp; \nearrow \searrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                        \\\
                        X &amp;\Downarrow&amp; Y
                        \\\
                        \&amp; \searrow \nearrow_{g}
                        }
                        \\,.
            %p
              The unbulleted version of groupoids are also called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-types"} homotopy 1-types
              (or often just their
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              are called this way.) Below we generalize this to arbitrary homotopy types (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KanComplexesAsHomotopyTypes"}
          #MappingGroupoid.num_example
            %h6#example_8 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              two groupoids, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} mapping groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
