                homotopies between such.
          #HomotopyEquivalenceOfGroupoids.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"}> homotopy-
              )
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
              is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{K}
              which has a left and right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
              up to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
          #BZIsPiSOne.num_example
            %h6#example_9 Example
            %p The map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z} \stackrel{}{\to} \Pi(S^1)
            %p
              which picks any point and sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
              to the loop based at that point which winds around
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              times, is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
          #DiscreteGroupoidIsDijointUnioonOfDeloopings.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Assuming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              in the ambient
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              groupoids, example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopingGroupoid"}
              – a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The statement of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiscreteGroupoidIsDijointUnioonOfDeloopings"}
              becomes false as when we pass to groupoids that are equipped with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometric
              structure. This is the reason why for discrete geometry all
              = succeed "-type" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons
              = succeed "-type" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-models"} AKSZ sigma-models
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
              is usefully discussed in terms of groupoid technology, in particular since the choice of equivalence in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiscreteGroupoidIsDijointUnioonOfDeloopings"}
              is not canonical.
          #HomotopyFiberProductOfGroupoids.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Given two morphisms of groupoids
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi g
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{f}{\to} B \stackrel{g}{\leftarrow} Y
              their
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %munder
                              %mo ×
                              %mi B
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \underset{B}{\times} Y
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\underset{g}{\to}&amp; B
                    }
            %p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                            %munder
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi B
                                  %mo •
                            %msubsup
                              %mi B
                              %mo •
                              %mi I
                            %munder
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi B
                                  %mo •
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi B
                              %mo •
                              %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi ev
                                  %mn 0
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ev
                                    %mn 1
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X_\bullet \underset{B_\bullet}{\times} B^I_\bullet
                    \\underset{B_\bullet}{\times} Y_\bullet
                    \&amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; X_\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f_\bullet}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; B^I_\bullet &amp;\underset{(ev_0)_\bullet}{\to}&amp; B_\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{(ev_1)_\bullet}}
                    \\\
                    Y_\bullet &amp;\underset{g_\bullet}{\to}&amp; B_\bullet
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence the ordinary iterated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space"} path space
              groupoid, as indicated.
          #FiberProductsOfGroupoidsComponentwise.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              An ordinary fiber product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \underset{B_\bullet}{\times}Y_\bullet
              of groupoids is given simply by the fiber product of the underlying sets of objects and morphisms:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X_\bullet \underset{B_\bullet}{\times}Y_\bullet)_i
                    \=
                    X_i \underset{B_i}{\times} Y_i
                    \\,.
          #PullbackOfEGGroupoidAsHomotopyFiberProduct.num_example
            %h6#example_10 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{B}G
              a map into its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
              of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
