                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; [\Pi(S^1), \mathbf{Fields}]
                  }
          %p
            The 2-dimensional composition of such processes, again by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            yields values on all higher spheres
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
